ect {:answer/id #uuid "6f1359a9-e2b2-535c-b05b-25bfab690331" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045499 :db/ident :answer.type/text} :answer/value "false" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186453652} :answer-field/id #uuid "142c805d-e505-5385-a031-31ee4017ce5c" :answer-field/key "III" :answer-field/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186408166 :db/ident :answer-field.type/checkbox} :db/id #edb/ref 17592186454576} {:answer-field/choices [{:answer/id #uuid "a729f994-14c9-52ba-bb3e-944dfe6019ee" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045499 :db/ident :answer.type/text} :answer/value "false" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186453654} {:answer/id #uuid "195487bd-bfd6-5cbd-b556-5442da419935" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045499 :db/ident :answer.type/text} :answer/value "true" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186453655}] :answer-field/correct {:answer/id #uuid "195487bd-bfd6-5cbd-b556-5442da419935" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045499 :db/ident :answer.type/text} :answer/value "true" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186453655} :answer-field/id #uuid "7d74078e-403c-53bb-b600-78b7e20a550f" :answer-field/key "IV" :answer-field/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186408166 :db/ident :answer-field.type/checkbox} :db/id #edb/ref 17592186454577}] :question/difficulty {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045485 :db/ident :question.difficulty/easy} :question/id #uuid "fb9b0e1b-3e64-5482-b003-6352af7b5cae" :question/math-academy-id "q-183396" :question/problem "$\\,$ If $A⊂B,$ then $A\\cap \\overset{―}{B}=∅.$\n\nWhich of the following statements are true regarding the implication above?\n\nSelect all that apply.\n\n- **I.** $A\\cap \\overset{―}{B}=∅$ is a **necessary** condition for $A⊂B$\n- **II.** $A⊂B$ is a **necessary** condition for $A\\cap \\overset{―}{B}=∅$\n- **III.** $A\\cap \\overset{―}{B}=∅$ is a **sufficient** condition for $A⊂B$\n- **IV.** $A⊂B$ is a **sufficient** condition for $A\\cap \\overset{―}{B}=∅$" :question/worked-solution "Given that the implication $S⇒N$ is true, we have the following:\n\n- $S$ being true *guarantees* that $N$ must also be true. Therefore, $S$ is a *sufficient condition* for $N.$\n\n- For $S$ to be true, it is *necessary* that $N$ is true. Therefore, $N$ is a *necessary condition* for $S.$ However, note that $N$ being true does *not* guarantee that $S$ is true.\n\nThese ideas can be summarized as follows:\n\n$$\n\\text{S}\\text{ufficient}\\,⇒\\,\\text{N}\\text{ecessary}.\n$$\n\n  \n\nIn our case, \n\n$$\n{{(\\,A⊂B\\,)}_{⏟}}_{\\text{sufficient}}\\,⇒\\,{{(\\,A\\cap \\overset{―}{B}=∅\\,)}_{⏟}}_{\\text{necessary}}\n$$\n\nis a true statement. Therefore:\n\n- Statement I is true. $A\\cap \\overset{―}{B}=∅$ is a **necessary** condition for $A⊂B.$\n\n- Statement IV is true. $A⊂B$ is a **sufficient** condition for $A\\cap \\overset{―}{B}=∅.$\n\nTherefore, the correct answer is \"I and IV only.\""}] [{:db/id #edb/ref 17592186420986 :knowledge-point/_questions [{:db/id #edb/ref 17592186054634 :knowledge-point/id #uuid "a6128eca-7f76-5386-9d67-d81db2943eeb" :knowledge-point/title "Computing a Cartesian Product"}] :question/answer-fields [{:answer-field/choices [{:answer/id #uuid "c3f010aa-4909-563a-a1c6-026ea372b9eb" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045499 :db/ident :answer.type/text} :answer/value "false" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186453610} {:answer/id #uuid "cc594cdc-9b20-5045-955a-b97073ccd9b3" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045499 :db/ident :answer.type/text} :answer/value "true" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186453611}] :answer-field/correct {:answer/id #uuid "c3f010aa-4909-563a-a1c6-026ea372b9eb" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045499 :db/ident :answer.type/text} :answer/value "false" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186453610} :answer-field/id #uuid "17837e49-2464-5649-bf83-90cccc331115" :answer-field/key "I" :answer-field/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186408166 :db/ident :answer-field.type/checkbox} :db/id #edb/ref 17592186454555} {:answer-field/choices [{:answer/id #uuid "0283c69d-345c-50d3-b197-80ce0b36bc50" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045499 :db/ident :answer.type/text} :answer/value "false" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186453612} {:answer/id #uuid "590b75d7-bead-582d-af00-04e682417e08" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045499 :db/ident :answer.type/text} :answer/value "true" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186453613}] :answer-field/correct {:answer/id #uuid "590b75d7-bead-582d-af00-04e682417e08" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045499 :db/ident :answer.type/text} :answer/value "true" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186453613} :answer-field/id #uuid "e96ebacd-74a3-5c9f-b150-1a708db2e23f" :answer-field/key "II" :answer-field/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186408166 :db/ident :answer-field.type/checkbox} :db/id #edb/ref 17592186454556} {:answer-field/choices [{:answer/id #uuid "ebbdbdd3-efff-5a4d-9fc3-2d71e2dbcfa6" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045499 :db/ident :answer.type/text} :answer/value "false" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186453614} {:answer/id #uuid "f355dabd-1bbd-5943-83a4-5e88ec291b6e" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045499 :db/ident :answer.type/text} :answer/value "true" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186453615}] :answer-field/correct {:answer/id #uuid "f355dabd-1bbd-5943-83a4-5e88ec291b6e" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045499 :db/ident :answer.type/text} :answer/value "true" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186453615} :answer-field/id #uuid "4c6c14f0-7877-5cdc-9923-b920790e1206" :answer-field/key "III" :answer-field/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186408166 :db/ident :answer-field.type/checkbox} :db/id #edb/ref 17592186454557}] :question/difficulty {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045485 :db/ident :question.difficulty/easy} :question/id #uuid "1f4365e0-4fb2-5b82-b78f-2c814bc881e5" :question/math-academy-id "q-182014" :question/problem "For the sets $A=\\{0,1,2\\},$ $B=\\{4,6,8\\},$ and $C=A\\times B,$ determine which of the following statements are true.\n\nSelect all that apply.\n\n- **I.** $(0,2)\\in C$\n\n- **II.** $(1,8)\\in C$\n\n- **III.** $(0,6)\\in C$" :question/worked-solution "The Cartesian product $A\\times B$ consists of all ordered pairs whose first coordinate belongs to $A$ and whose second coordinate belongs to $B.$\n\nIn this case, the schematic for $A\\times B$ is shown below.\n\n![](images/12/12d1b94cc6d53954a9c164bd069f77fcddc7a46de2c1701c1f4cdfc608eef185.png)\n\nHence, the set $C=A\\times B$ is given by\n\n$$\nC={(0,4),(0,6),(0,8),(1,4),(1,6),(1,8),(2,4),(2,6),(2,8)}.\n$$\n\nTherefore, the correct answer is \"II and III only.\""}] [{:db/id #edb/ref 17592186421406 :knowledge-point/_questions [{:db/id #edb/ref 17592186152066 :knowledge-point/id #uuid "b70dd396-b01a-51e6-a52c-8ff729f48c45" :knowledge-point/title "Determining Whether a Standard Relation Is an Equivalence"}] :question/answer-fields [{:answer-field/choices [{:answer/id #uuid "8d2ecaf5-e9a0-5ac2-9183-69db4543a66a" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045499 :db/ident :answer.type/text} :answer/value "false" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186453742} {:answer/id #uuid "9c2e347c-bbd6-5423-9565-80267bb6eaab" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045499 :db/ident :answer.type/text} :answer/value "true" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186453743}] :answer-field/correct {:answer/id #uuid "9c2e347c-bbd6-5423-9565-80267bb6eaab" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045499 :db/ident :answer.type/text} :answer/value "true" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186453743} :answer-field/id #uuid "57f53dd6-66c3-5316-bb4d-346cf5f0671c" :answer-field/key "I" :answer-field/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186408166 :db/ident :answer-field.type/checkbox} :db/id #edb/ref 17592186454621} {:answer-field/choices [{:answer/id #uuid "369ec3ac-7594-53e7-86b1-8ed81e593cd1" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045499 :db/ident :answer.type/text} :answer/value "false" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186453744} {:answer/id #uuid "ece1440a-f636-5a14-bd79-3859bd270e7b" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045499 :db/ident :answer.type/text} :answer/value "true" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186453745}] :answer-field/correct {:answer/id #uuid "ece1440a-f636-5a14-bd79-3859bd270e7b" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045499 :db/ident :answer.type/text} :answer/value "true" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186453745} :answer-field/id #uuid "8397c69c-e704-5336-ab46-63a2a420b12b" :answer-field/key "II" :answer-field/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186408166 :db/ident :answer-field.type/checkbox} :db/id #edb/ref 17592186454622} {:answer-field/choices [{:answer/id #uuid "6cb40e47-129b-5e8c-96ec-f9dffe1c80b2" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045499 :db/ident :answer.type/text} :answer/value "false" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186453746} {:answer/id #uuid "78de381b-cb88-517b-9e8f-479328b7da2f" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045499 :db/ident :answer.type/text} :answer/value "true" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186453747}] :answer-field/correct {:answer/id #uuid "78de381b-cb88-517b-9e8f-479328b7da2f" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045499 :db/ident :answer.type/text} :answer/value "true" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186453747} :answer-field/id #uuid "0424cae6-af37-5568-967e-b8349f54700c" :answer-field/key "III" :answer-field/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186408166 :db/ident :answer-field.type/checkbox} :db/id #edb/ref 17592186454623} {:answer-field/choices [{:answer/id #uuid "8ee7950d-2e0f-561b-a855-dcda433c326e" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045499 :db/ident :answer.type/text} :answer/value "false" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186453748} {:answer/id #uuid "52ec55e9-022a-5936-b3fd-bf3dd4db01ab" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045499 :db/ident :answer.type/text} :answer/value "true" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186453749}] :answer-field/correct {:answer/id #uuid "52ec55e9-022a-5936-b3fd-bf3dd4db01ab" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045499 :db/ident :answer.type/text} :answer/value "true" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186453749} :answer-field/id #uuid "347ab12e-5830-50c8-b5fe-11a0cb0e2867" :answer-field/key "IV" :answer-field/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186408166 :db/ident :answer-field.type/checkbox} :db/id #edb/ref 17592186454624}] :question/difficulty {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045485 :db/ident :question.difficulty/easy} :question/id #uuid "1b086cc6-e229-5377-bb89-5a8ff879bb27" :question/math-academy-id "q-214271" :question/problem "Consider the following relation defined on the set $P(A),$ where $A={1,2,3,…,10}.$ \n\n$$\nX\\,R\\,Y\\,⇔\\,|X|=|Y|\n$$\n\n Which of the following statements are true?\n\nSelect all that apply.\n\n- **I.** $R$ is reflexive\n- **II.** $R$ is symmetric\n- **III.** $R$ is transitive\n- **IV.** $R$ is an equivalence relation" :question/worked-solution "Given a relation $R$ on a set $A$:\n\n- $R$ is reflexive if and only if for all $x\\in A,$ $x\\,R\\,x.$\n\n- $R$ is symmetric if and only if for all $x,y\\in A,$ if $x\\,R\\,y,$ then $y\\,R\\,x.$\n\n- $R$ is transitive if and only if for all $x,y,z\\in A,$ if $x\\,R\\,y$ and $y\\,R\\,z,$ then $x\\,R\\,z.$\n\nIf $R$ is reflexive, symmetric, and transitive, then $R$ is an equivalence relation.\n\nLet's consider each of the properties in turn.\n\n- The relation $R$ is reflexive. For all $X\\in P(A),$ $|X|\\,=\\,|X|.$\n\n- The relation $R$ is symmetric. For all $X,Y\\in P(A),$ if $|X|\\,=\\,|Y|,$ then $|Y|=|X|.$\n\n- The relation $R$ is transitive. For all $X,Y,Z\\in P(A),$ if $|X|=|Y|$ and $|Y|=|Z|,$ then $|X|=|Z|.$\n\n- The relation $R$ is an equivalence relation since it's reflexive, symmetric, and transitive.\n\nTherefore, the correct answer is \"I, II, III, and IV only.\""}] [{:db/id #edb/ref 17592186421409 :knowledge-point/_questions [{:db/id #edb/ref 17592186152067 :knowledge-point/id #uuid "968df6ec-e87e-5770-9c11-e7c8d8a27e6c" :knowledge-point/title "Identifying Equivalence Relations on Finite Sets"}] :question/answer-fields [{:answer-field/choices [{:answer/id #uuid "4ce48c9f-99d9-5a57-a00b-4e4bf360757e" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045499 :db/ident :answer.type/text} :answer/value "false" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186453758} {:answer/id #uuid "14605bc1-af90-5790-a615-0b1a9fadf2a4" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045499 :db/ident :answer.type/text} :answer/value "true" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186453759}] :an